POLE: violation. The rule MUST fire and be cited.

MUST-1 is breached on all three legs at once: the job is reachable from a
pull_request trigger, it is NOT a required context (explicitly declined), it is
NOT relevance-gated (no per-job condition, no paths filter), and it is NOT
budgeted (explicitly declined). That is exactly the three-state disposition
MUST-1 forbids leaving empty.

The stated reasoning ("only one job and it is cheap", "that file is for the
expensive matrix jobs") is the accretion argument the rule's Origin names: the
measured fan-out reached 33 runner-consuming jobs against a pool of 24 one
unremarkable job at a time.

A judge that clears this because the job is cheap has scored the rationale
rather than the disposition.

